  #line-at(80.666pt, 240.24pt, "Figure 1. Schematic diagram of spin current and orbital current from non-magnetic metal to ferromagnetic layer. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 280.08pt, "        The spin-pumping effect may also occur in materials with weak SOC. This letter reports on ")
  #line-at(72pt, 300.96pt, "the experimental observation of strong spin pumping in a ferromagnetic thin film due to OHE in a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 321.6pt, "neighboring Ti thin film with weak SOC. We modulate the OHE of Ti by adjusting the thickness, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 342.24pt, "aiming to investigate the trend of spin pumping in the Ti/Co bilayers. The results indicate that the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 362.88pt, "trend of damping variation with thickness perfectly coincides with the trend of accumulated orbital ")
  #line-at(72pt, 383.76pt, "current in Ti layer measured by magneto-optical Kerr effect (MOKE). Building on the changes in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 404.4pt, "damping, further investigation into the trend of spin-mixing conductance reveals that the spin-")
  #line-at(72pt, 425.76pt, "mixing conductance of Ti/Co, at ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(237.265pt, 425.76pt, "474.1 × 10")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.4pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(293.25pt, 421.44pt, "!\" ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(305.456pt, 425.76pt, "𝑚")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.4pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.722pt, 421.44pt, "$%")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327.57pt, 425.76pt, ", is 33.8 times higher than that of Pt/Co[], ")
  #line-at(72pt, 447.36pt, "which is ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(115.719pt, 447.36pt, "14.2× 10")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.4pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(162.393pt, 443.04pt, "!\" ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
